<!DOCTYPE properties SYSTEM "http://java.sun.com/dtd/properties.dtd">
<properties>
    <entry key="defaultServiceAccessInformationTimerInterval">10</entry>
    <!-- How long, in milliseconds, the Media Session Handler waits for the network of a Data Network (dataNetworkName of a metrics
         reporting configuration) before it reports the Data Network as not available. No clause gives a value; this is the default,
         the operator of the device may change it. -->
    <entry key="dataNetworkRequestTimeout">5000</entry>
    <!-- How old, in seconds, the last known location of the UE may be when the geographic areas of a locationFilter (TS 26.510 table 8.7.3.1-1)
         are checked. No clause gives a value; this is the default, the operator of the device may change it. -->
    <entry key="locationMaxAgeSeconds">300</entry>
    <!-- The client credentials grant (RFC 6749 clause 4.4) with which the Media Session Handler obtains the access token for the Media AF
         at M5 (TS 26.510 clause 7.4.3), when the application gave none to createMediaDeliverySession, and renews it when the Media AF
         answers 401 invalid_token. Empty token URL or client identifier: no token is obtained. -->
    <entry key="oauthTokenUrl"></entry>
    <entry key="oauthClientId"></entry>
    <entry key="oauthClientSecret"></entry>
    <entry key="oauthScope"></entry>
    <!-- The credentials of the Media Session Handler at the MQTT broker of the notification channel (TS 26.510 clause 10.2.1: "The MQTT broker
         shall use appropriate client authentication mechanisms, such as a token-based authentication mechanism (JWT) [51] to secure access
         to the notification channel."). The password is the token when the broker uses one. Empty: the client connects without credentials. -->
    <entry key="mqttUsername"></entry>
    <entry key="mqttPassword"></entry>
    <!-- The conformance profiles (URIs, comma separated) of the Media Entry Points that this device plays (TS 26.512 clause 4.7.2.1). An entry
         point that declares profiles, none of them listed here, is not offered to the Media Stream Handler. Empty: all profiles. -->
    <entry key="supportedProfiles"></entry>
    <!-- Reports that the Media AF answers with 503 are stored and sent again (TS 26.510 clauses 5.3.5.2 and 5.3.6.2: "should store outstanding
         ... reports and reattempt submission when the endpoint later becomes available"). reportRetrySeconds: the wait when the answer has no
         Retry-After header; maxStoredReports: how many are kept per reporting procedure, the oldest are dropped. No clause gives either
         value; these are defaults, the operator of the device may change them. -->
    <entry key="reportRetrySeconds">30</entry>
    <entry key="maxStoredReports">10</entry>
</properties>